  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2035(a), transfers of life insurance policies within three years of the decedent''s death cause the full proceeds to be pulled back into the gross estate. Palmer transferred the policy in March 2024 and died in January 2026, less than three years later, so the entire death benefit is includable.
Wrong (A): The completed transfer does not shield the proceeds. Section 2035 specifically overrides normal transfer rules for life insurance policies transferred within three years of death.
Wrong (C): There is no pro-rata inclusion based on premiums paid before versus after transfer. The entire proceeds are included under the three-year rule.
