UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 2503(b), the annual gift tax exclusion applies only to gifts of present interests, meaning the donee has an immediate right to use, possess, or enjoy the property. Crummey withdrawal powers are often used to convert future interests into present interests.
Wrong (B): A future interest is the opposite of what qualifies. The annual exclusion specifically excludes future interests such as reversions and remainders.
Wrong (C): A vested remainder interest is still a future interest for gift tax purposes because the donee cannot access it until a later date.
Wrong (D): An income interest in a trust may or may not qualify depending on whether the beneficiary has a present right to receive distributions.$EXPL$
