  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 2040(a), for joint tenancies between non-spouses, the full property value is included in the decedent''s gross estate except to the extent the surviving tenant can prove their own contribution. Monroe contributed $150,000 of the $750,000 purchase price, so $600,000 is included in Caldwell''s estate.
Wrong (B): The 50% rule under Section 2040(b) applies only to joint tenancies between spouses. Non-spouse joint tenancies use the contribution-based test instead.
Wrong (C): Including the full $750,000 ignores Monroe''s provable contribution. Section 2040(a) reduces inclusion by the survivor''s documented share.
Wrong (D): Monroe''s contribution of $150,000 is subtracted from the total, not included as the estate''s share. The estate includes Caldwell''s portion, not Monroe''s.$EXPL$
