-- Q5528: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2001(b), the estate tax base equals the taxable estate plus adjusted taxable gifts. The taxable estate is $12,000,000 minus $1,000,000 in deductions = $11,000,000. Adding the $3,500,000 in lifetime taxable gifts produces an estate tax base of $14,500,000.
Wrong (A): $11,000,000 reflects only the taxable estate without adding back lifetime taxable gifts, which the unified transfer tax system requires to determine the correct marginal bracket.
Wrong (C): $11,200,000 incorrectly adds the $200,000 in gift taxes paid to the taxable estate. Previously paid gift taxes reduce the tentative tax, not the tax base.
Wrong (D): $15,500,000 incorrectly adds the full gross estate ($12,000,000) to gifts ($3,500,000) without subtracting deductions first.$EXPL$
