-- Q5553: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 2032A, qualifying real property may be valued at current use rather than highest and best use, subject to an indexed statutory cap ($1,390,000 for recent years). Although the actual difference here is $1,800,000, the cap limits the reduction. Recapture tax under Section 2032A(c) applies if qualified use ceases within 10 years of death.
Wrong (A): This ignores both the statutory cap on the reduction amount and the mandatory recapture provision. The full $1,800,000 difference cannot be claimed.
Wrong (B): Section 2032A provides a permanent valuation reduction, not a tax deferral. The reduced value is used to compute the gross estate directly.
Wrong (D): The farm remains a taxable asset included in the gross estate. It is simply valued at a lower amount under the special use election, not excluded entirely.$EXPL$
