  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 7872, a below-market loan between family members results in an imputed gift equal to the foregone interest. The foregone interest is $200,000 x 5.2% = $10,400, treated as a deemed gift from Thornberry to Keating for 2026.
Wrong (A): Section 7872 specifically applies to gift loans between family members. Family loans are not exempt from imputed interest rules when they are below-market.
Wrong (B): The $19,000 annual exclusion is a separate provision that may offset the gift but does not limit the imputed amount. The imputed gift is calculated based on the AFR, not the exclusion.
