-- Q5564: Estate and Gift Tax [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 2503(b), the annual exclusion applies only to gifts of present interests giving the donee an immediate right to use, possess, or enjoy the property. A remainder interest is a future interest because the donee cannot access it until a later event, so it does not qualify for the exclusion.
Wrong (A): A cash deposit into the donee''s bank account is a present interest because the donee has immediate access and use of the funds.
Wrong (B): Publicly traded stock transferred directly to the donee is a present interest because the donee can immediately sell or hold the shares.
Wrong (C): A trust with immediate withdrawal rights (Crummey powers) converts what would be a future interest into a present interest qualifying for the exclusion.$EXPL$
