  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 509(a)(3), an organization qualifies as a public charity if it is organized and operated exclusively to support one or more specified public charities. Sunrise Support Services meets this test by operating exclusively to raise funds for Sunrise Community Hospital.
Wrong (B): The Section 509(a)(3) supporting organization classification provides an alternative path to public charity status that does not require broad public support.
Wrong (C): Section 509(a)(1) applies to organizations that themselves receive public support or are churches, schools, or hospitals. A fundraising entity for a hospital does not independently qualify under this section.
Wrong (D): A private operating foundation actively conducts its own charitable programs. An organization that solely raises funds for another charity is a supporting organization, not an operating foundation.$EXPL$
