  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 6072(e), Form 990 must be filed by the 15th day of the 5th month after the organization''s tax year ends. For a calendar-year organization, the deadline is May 15. Extensions of up to six months are available using Form 8868.
Wrong (A): March 15 is the filing deadline for partnerships (Form 1065) and S corporations (Form 1120-S), not for tax-exempt organizations filing Form 990.
Wrong (B): April 15 is the deadline for individual income tax returns (Form 1040) and C corporation returns (Form 1120), not for exempt organization returns.
