-- Q7726: Tax-Exempt Organizations [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 509(a)(1) and Section 170(b)(1)(A)(vi), the one-third support test requires that at least one-third of total support come from governmental units and the general public. Here, $120,000 / $400,000 = 30%, which falls below the 33.3% threshold, so the organization fails the test.
Wrong (A): Total support exceeding $100,000 is irrelevant to the one-third support test. The test measures the proportion of public and governmental support relative to total support.
Wrong (B): Receiving some government funding does not automatically satisfy the test. The public and government support must equal at least one-third of total support.
Wrong (C): While concentrated support from one donor is a concern, the specific disqualification is that public support fails the one-third threshold, not merely that one donor provides a large share.$EXPL$
