-- Q7728: Tax-Exempt Organizations [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 513(f), bingo game income is excluded from UBIT when the games are legal and conducted in a jurisdiction where commercial bingo operations are not ordinarily carried on. This prevents exempt organizations from competing with taxable bingo businesses.
Wrong (B): No dollar threshold applies to the bingo exclusion. The test is geographic, based on whether commercial bingo is ordinarily conducted in the same jurisdiction.
Wrong (C): There is no frequency limitation in Section 513(f). The exclusion applies whether bingo is held weekly or monthly, provided the other conditions are met.
Wrong (D): The exclusion does not require that only board members operate the games. Volunteer staffing is relevant to the separate Section 513(a)(1) volunteer exclusion, not the bingo exclusion.$EXPL$
