-- Q8113: Tax-Exempt Organizations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 513(f), bingo games are specifically excluded from UBIT if the games are legal under state and local law and commercial bingo is not ordinarily carried on in the jurisdiction. This statutory exclusion applies regardless of frequency or revenue amount.
Wrong (B): The regularly-carried-on analysis under Section 512 does not override the specific bingo exclusion in Section 513(f). When the bingo exclusion applies, the general UBIT test is irrelevant.
Wrong (C): The volunteer exclusion under Section 513(a)(1) is a separate provision. The bingo exclusion under Section 513(f) is the primary statutory authority and does not depend on volunteer staffing.
Wrong (D): Relatedness to charitable purpose is part of the general UBIT test, but the Section 513(f) bingo exclusion is a specific statutory carve-out that applies independently of the relatedness analysis.$EXPL$
